// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6233 Add macOS rule for browser credential database query via a database CLI utility
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6233
// Pull request author: clivoa
// Change: new rule
// Title: Browser Credential Database Query Via Database CLI Utility - MacOS
// Sigma ID: 4e0d4a1c-8d2b-4d19-9c1e-2a4f8e6b7c35
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: clivoa
// Date: 2026-08-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1555.003, T1539
// Description: Detects a command line database client such as "sqlite3" or "duckdb" reading a browser
//   credential, cookie or autofill database. Chromium stores these in "Login Data", "Cookies" and
//   "Web Data", and Firefox stores them in "cookies.sqlite" and "key4.db". Because "sqlite3" ships
//   with macOS and is signed by Apple, this technique lets an attacker read the databases without
//   dropping an unsigned binary on the host. Opening the database through a "file:" URI with the
//   "immutable=1" parameter also avoids the lock that a running browser holds, so the browser does
//   not have to be killed first.
// False positives:
//   - Backup, migration or browser forensics tooling that reads these databases through a database CLI utility
//   - Administrators or developers inspecting their own browser profile from a terminal
// References:
//   - https://www.loobins.io/binaries/sqlite3/
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/threat-intelligence/clipping-silver-sparrows-wings/
//   - https://www.jamf.com/blog/crashstealer-macos-infostealer-analysis/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6c68012a51ecabd8a9b3f518662cc95f7dde06c0/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_browser_credential_db_query_via_db_cli.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/sqlite3" or FolderPath endswith "/duckdb") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "Login Data" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Web Data" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Cookies" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cookies.sqlite" or ProcessCommandLine contains "key4.db")
